            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Practice MCQs for the whole of Unit 9 (Division of Polynomials), arranged by the unit's sections. Each question has one correct answer with a short explanation that shows the working."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "9.1 Polynomial Function"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "1 The degree of the polynomial \\(4x^{5} - 3x^{2} + 7\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(5\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(4\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(7\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "The degree is the highest power of \\(x\\), here \\(5\\) (4 is the leading coefficient, not the degree).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "is called the degree of the polynomial"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "2 Which one of the following is a polynomial in \\(x\\)?",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x^{-2} + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(x^{3} - 2x + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(\\sqrt{x} + 3\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{x} + x\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "In a polynomial every power of \\(x\\) is a non-negative integer. \\(x^{-2}\\), \\(\\sqrt{x} = x^{1/2}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{x} = x^{-1}\\) are not allowed.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "is a non-negative integer and the coefficients"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "3 When \\(f(x)\\) is divided by \\(x - 3\\), the quotient is \\(x^{2} + 1\\) and the remainder is \\(4\\). Then \\(f(x)\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x^{3} - 3x^{2} + x - 7\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(x^{3} + 3x^{2} + x + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x^{3} - 3x^{2} + x + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(x^{3} - 3x^{2} + 4\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "Dividend = Divisor \\(\\times\\) Quotient + Remainder: \\((x - 3)(x^{2} + 1) + 4 = x^{3} - 3x^{2} + x - 3 + 4 = x^{3} - 3x^{2} + x + 1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "This unit studies the division of one polynomial by another to find the quotient and the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "4 When a polynomial is divided by a linear polynomial \\(x - a\\), the remainder is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "a linear polynomial"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "always zero"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "a quadratic polynomial"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "a constant"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "d",
            "explanation": "We stop when the degree of the remainder is less than the degree of the divisor; the divisor has degree 1, so the remainder has degree 0, a constant.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "This unit studies the division of one polynomial by another to find the quotient and the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "5 The quotient when \\(x^{2} + 5x + 7\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x + 7\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(x + 3\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x - 3\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(x + 5\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "\\(x^{2} + 5x + 7 = (x + 2)(x + 3) + 1\\): quotient \\(x + 3\\), remainder \\(1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "This unit studies the division of one polynomial by another to find the quotient and the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "6 When \\(2x^{3} + x^{2} - 5x + 2\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\), the quotient is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(2x^{2} + 5x + 5\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(2x^{2} - 3x - 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(2x^{2} + 3x + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(2x^{2} - 3x + 1\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "d",
            "explanation": "\\((x + 2)(2x^{2} - 3x + 1) = 2x^{3} + x^{2} - 5x + 2\\), so the quotient is \\(2x^{2} - 3x + 1\\) and the remainder is 0.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "This unit studies the division of one polynomial by another to find the quotient and the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "7 When \\(x^{3} + 2x^{2} + 3x + 4\\) is divided by \\(x^{2} + 1\\), the remainder is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(2x + 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x + 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(4x + 6\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "\\((x^{2} + 1)(x + 2) = x^{3} + 2x^{2} + x + 2\\); subtracting from the dividend leaves \\(2x + 2\\), whose degree is less than 2.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "a5a377ae-2e8e-56de-9d7f-0331f52ed3fc",
              "quote": "This unit studies the division of one polynomial by another to find the quotient and the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "9.1.1 Remainder Theorem"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "8 The remainder when \\(x^{3} - 2x^{2} + 4\\) is divided by \\(x - 3\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(-41\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(4\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(13\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(31\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "Remainder \\(= f(3) = 27 - 18 + 4 = 13\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "9 The remainder when \\(2x^{4} - x + 5\\) is divided by \\(x + 1\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(6\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(4\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(8\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "d",
            "explanation": "\\(x + 1 = x - (-1)\\), so the remainder is \\(f(-1) = 2 + 1 + 5 = 8\\). (\\(f(1) = 6\\) is the sign slip.)",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "10 The remainder when \\(f(x)\\) is divided by \\(x + a\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(f(a)\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(-f(a)\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(f(-a)\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(f(0)\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "\\(x + a = x - (-a)\\), so by the remainder theorem the remainder is \\(f(-a)\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "11 If \\(x^{3} + kx - 4\\) leaves remainder \\(6\\) when divided by \\(x - 2\\), then \\(k\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(-1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(3\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(5\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "\\(f(2) = 8 + 2k - 4 = 2k + 4 = 6\\), so \\(k = 1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "12 The remainder when \\(3x^{3} + 5x - 7\\) is divided by \\(x\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(-7\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(7\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(0\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "\\(x = x - 0\\), so the remainder is \\(f(0) = -7\\), the constant term.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "13 The remainder when \\(x^{50} + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 1\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(0\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(-2\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "\\(f(-1) = (-1)^{50} + 1 = 1 + 1 = 2\\) (an even power of \\(-1\\) is 1).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "14 The remainder when \\(x^{3} + 1\\) is divided by \\(x - \\frac{1}{2}\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{8}\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{4}\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{8}\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "d",
            "explanation": "\\(f\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{8} + 1 = \\frac{9}{8}\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "till no \\(x\\)-term exists in the remainder, then \\(f(a)\\) is the remainder."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "15 If \\(f(x)\\) leaves remainder \\(5\\) when divided by \\(x - 2\\), then \\(f(2)\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(0\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(5\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(-5\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "From \\(f(x) = (x - 2)q(x) + 5\\), putting \\(x = 2\\): \\(f(2) = 0 + 5 = 5\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "d9487255-a0bd-5318-bf5c-31cfa1ef4685",
              "quote": "Hence remainder \\(= f(a)\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "9.1.2 Factor Theorem"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "16 \\(x - a\\) is a factor of \\(f(x)\\) if and only if:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(f(a) = 0\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(f(-a) = 0\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(f(0) = a\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(f(a) = a\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "Factor theorem: \\(x - a\\) is a factor of \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "17 Which one of the following is a factor of \\(x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 5x + 6\\)?",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x - 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(x + 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x + 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(x + 3\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "\\(f(-2) = -8 - 8 + 10 + 6 = 0\\), so \\(x + 2\\) is a factor. \\(f(2) = -4\\), \\(f(-1) = 8\\), \\(f(-3) = -24\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "18 If \\(x - 1\\) is a factor of \\(x^{3} + kx^{2} - 3x + 4\\), then \\(k\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(-2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(-8\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(6\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "\\(f(1) = 1 + k - 3 + 4 = k + 2 = 0\\), so \\(k = -2\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "19 If \\(x + 2\\) is a factor of \\(x^{2} + px - 6\\), then \\(p\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(-1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(5\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(-5\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "\\(f(-2) = 4 - 2p - 6 = -2 - 2p = 0\\), so \\(p = -1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "20 If \\(x = -3\\) is a root of \\(f(x) = 0\\), then a factor of \\(f(x)\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x - 3\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(3x\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x + \\frac{1}{3}\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(x + 3\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "d",
            "explanation": "\\(x - a\\) is a factor iff \\(x = a\\) is a root; with \\(a = -3\\) the factor is \\(x - (-3) = x + 3\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is the root of the polynomial equation"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "21 \\(x - 1\\) is a factor of \\(3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + x + k\\) when \\(k\\) is:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(-1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(9\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(-9\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "b",
            "explanation": "\\(f(1) = 3 - 5 + 1 + k = k - 1 = 0\\), so \\(k = 1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "22 If \\(x - 1\\) and \\(x + 1\\) are factors of \\(x^{3} + ax^{2} + bx - 2\\), then:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(a = -2,\\ b = 1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(a = 1,\\ b = 0\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(a = 2,\\ b = -1\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(a = 2,\\ b = 1\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "c",
            "explanation": "\\(f(1) = a + b - 1 = 0\\) and \\(f(-1) = a - b - 3 = 0\\); adding, \\(2a = 4\\), so \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = -1\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "question",
            "prompt": "23 \\(x^{5} - 32\\) is exactly divisible by:",
            "options": [
              {
                "id": "a",
                "text": "\\(x - 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "b",
                "text": "\\(x + 2\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "c",
                "text": "\\(x - 4\\)"
              },
              {
                "id": "d",
                "text": "\\(x + 4\\)"
              }
            ],
            "answer_id": "a",
            "explanation": "\\(f(2) = 32 - 32 = 0\\), so \\(x - 2\\) is a factor. \\(f(-2) = -64\\), \\(f(4) = 992\\), \\(f(-4) = -1056\\).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "428febb3-efcc-5cb9-94fc-fe0456d179f9",
              "quote": "is a factor of the polynomial \\(f(x)\\) iff \\(f(a) = 0\\)."
            }
          },
          {
